<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Miguelist Portugal</h1><p class="st-meta">1828 CE – 1834 CE · capital Lisbon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The absolutist regime of King Miguel I, whose seizure of the throne in 1828 sparked Portugal's Liberal Wars.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-of-portugal">John VI</a>'s death in 1826 his heir Pedro, emperor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>, granted Portugal a constitutional Charter and abdicated for his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-ii-of-portugal">Maria II</a>, naming his brother Miguel regent. In 1828 Miguel, backed by absolutists and the Church, had the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> proclaim him king.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Miguel abolished the Charter and ruled as an absolute monarch, persecuting liberals, many of whom fled abroad or to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azores">Azores</a>. He enjoyed popular support in the countryside and among the clergy, but most European powers refused to recognise him. The liberals held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terceira">Terceira</a> and formed a government in exile.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Pedro returned from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>, landed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> in 1832 and endured a long siege before liberal forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> in 1833. Miguel surrendered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concession-of-evoramonte">Concession of Evoramonte</a> in May 1834 and went into permanent exile, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-ii-of-portugal">Maria II</a> was restored to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1828 CE – 1834 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.08%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1828 CE – 1834 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lisbon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Miguel I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Absolutist Portugal under Miguel I</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1831&amp;focus=miguelist-portugal" aria-label="Miguelist Portugal on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4453 789 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Miguelist Portugal lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4773 1045L4773 1045"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4773 1045h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lisbon. <a href="/atlas?year=1831&amp;focus=miguelist-portugal">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
